        "original_id": "9017e448-e855-5766-b73f-7740198c1fc1",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Dave Grohl, Pat Smear\n- Music Groups: Foo Fighters\n- Songs: \"These Days\"\n- Albums: \"Wasting Light\"\n- Companies: RCA Records\n\nFacts:\n- \"The Colour and the Shape\" was released in 1997, and \"Wasting Light\" was the first Foo Fighters album to feature rhythm guitarist Pat Smear since that album.\n- On April 12, 2011, Foo Fighters released their seventh studio album \"Wasting Light\" on RCA Records.\n- \"Wasting Light\" made Foo Fighters a five-piece band.\n- \"These Days\" is a song from \"Wasting Light\" by the American rock band Foo Fighters.\n- \"These Days\" was released as the third single from \"Wasting Light\", and it was the fourth single in the UK.\n- Dave Grohl stated that \"These Days\" is his favourite song that he has ever written.",
